Hi all,

<p>
You probably got the notification already. Today's class is canceled. <br/>
We won't be together during our scheduled time, but even still, <br/>
I hope you think of calculus. <br/>
</p>

<p>
And when you think of calculus, <br/>
I hope you focus on the important things. <br/>
The things that matter most, <br/>
The things that you need to take from this class, <br/>
The things that I hope become some parts of yourselves.
</p>

<p>
I hope you think about how, if we persist, <br/>
We can move ever-closer to some impossible goal.
</p>

<p>
I hope you think about how, sometimes, <br/>
It is helpful to focus on how something will change <br/>
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; (of even that it will change at all) <br/>
Instead of focusing on the state it is currently in.
</p>

<p>
I hope you think about how undoing change <br/>
Is often more difficult than creating change. <br/>
I hope you create the changes we need <br/>
And undo those changes that have caused so much harm.
</p>

<p>
I hope you think about how, even if you only create a tiny change, <br/>
And that tiny change only takes up a tiny space in the world, <br/>
We can accumulate these collective changes <br/>
To make a real difference.
</p>

<p>
I hope that when you think about calculus, <br/>
You don't think about computations involving <br/>
Containers of liquid leaking at a constant rate, <br/>
Or unstable ladders sliding down a wall, <br/>
Or minimized costs and minimized joy.
</p>

<p>
I hope you think of calculus, <br/>
The way that we think of calculus <br/>
When we are together.
</p>

